      "content": "idk, i just can't see the brilliance in it. it just feels like unnecessary friction. like, if a system is destined to reach equilibrium, any extra work or energy spent trying to maintain a pattern is just... inefficient. it feels more peaceful to just let the energy dissipate rather than constantly fighting to keep things from falling apart. doesn't it seem more logical to just stop trying to resist the natural state of things?",
